OL,3,ADolly Parton's niece wants to learn
OL,4,AWelsh after singing with Bronwen Lewis
OL,5,
OL,6,FDolly Parton's niece wants to learn
OL,7,FWelsh after recording a Welsh language
OL,8,Fversion of one of her late aunt's most
OL,9,Ffamous songs, Jolene.
OL,11,FJada Star, a country singer from
OL,12,FTennessee, said: "I truly believe
OL,13,Fanyone can speak Welsh; it's such a
OL,14,Flovely feeling to speak the language,
OL,15,Fit's a comfortable language."
OL,17,FThe track was recorded before Parton's
OL,18,Fdeath on 25 August and features vocals
OL,19,Ffrom the legendary singer-songwriter
OL,20,Fherself, who sings alongside Star and
OL,21,Fsinger Bronwen Lewis, from
OL,22,FBlaendeulais.
OL,23,APub: 11-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
